 {
  "id": "rematch-minimap-zoom",
  "title": "Rematch Minimap Zoom",
  "author": "rematch-scripts",
  "description": "Draws a magnified copy of the minimap on top of the game. Zoom and focus point can be changed live from the menu, or with the ] and [ keys in game.",
  "instructions": "**How to use**\n1. Press **Download & add to menu**.\n2. In **Script menu** switch the script on (the first start installs the Python libraries; Python 3.10+ is required).\n3. Set **Region: left / top / width / height** so the box covers exactly the minimap on your screen (defaults are for 1920x1080). Region changes restart the script.\n4. Change **Zoom** and **Focus point** with the sliders. They apply instantly.\n5. In the game: **]** zooms in, **[** zooms out, and the **show/hide key** from the settings hides the overlay.\n6. Gamepad: hold **Back/View** and press D-pad Up (zoom in), Down (zoom out) or Left (show/hide).\n\nThe game must run in **Borderless / windowed** mode. The script only reads the screen image.",
  "version": 1,
